    <P Name="Name">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Helvetica&apos;; font-size:10px; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;This is the stability controller which implements a cascaded PIV controller. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;1. The first part generates an angular rate command based on an angular position error. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;2. The second part of the controller generates a torque command based on an angular rate error.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%; font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12px;&quot;&gt;The cascaded PIV controllers always stabilize with respect to the Attitude Commands (rad, rad/s) [3] setpoint. The Attitude Torques (Nm) [3] are added to the output of the cascaded PIV controllers to generate the Generalized Force (N, Nm) [4].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; line-height:100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</P>
    <P Name="Position">[108, 619, 867, 709]</P>
    <P Name="InternalMargins">[0, 0, 0, 0]</P>
    <P Name="FixedHeight">on</P>
    <P Name="FixedWidth">on</P>
    <P Name="HorizontalAlignment">left</P>
    <P Name="VerticalAlignment">top</P>
    <P Name="Interpreter">rich</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">-30</P>
  </Annotation>
  <Annotation SID="14029">
    <P Name="Name">This subsystem switches between Attitude Torques AND Attitude Commands depending on 
the value of the Mode signal: 
Mode = 1	=&gt; 		Torque mode, Attitude Commands are zeroed
Mode = 0	=&gt; 		Angle mode, Attitude Torques are zeroed</P>
    <P Name="Position">[-545, 640, -184, 705]</P>
    <P Name="InternalMargins">[0, 0, 0, 0]</P>
    <P Name="FixedHeight">on</P>
    <P Name="FixedWidth">on</P>
    <P Name="HorizontalAlignment">left</P>
    <P Name="VerticalAlignment">top</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">-1</P>
  </Annotation>
  <Annotation SID="14032">
    <P Name="Name">3. Safety Monitor </P>
    <P Name="Position">[-543, 896, -158, 991]</P>
    <P Name="InternalMargins">[0, 0, 0, 0]</P>
    <P Name="FixedHeight">on</P>
    <P Name="FixedWidth">on</P>
    <P Name="HorizontalAlignment">left</P>
