  <Annotation SID="13857">
    <P Name="Name">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Helvetica&apos;; font-size:10px; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Subsystem Description:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;Checking signals related to the current FSM state, initialization timer, motion capture system tracking flag, mission server communication status and battery level status. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;Monitoring the trigger signals from the joystick as well as if there is an issue with the joystick signal. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;Throttle monitoring, meant to give information about the commanded throttle (CMD Throttle) and the throttle calculated by the position controller (Ctrl Throttle).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;This subsystem is monitoring the current pose measurement from the motion capture system and generates flags when the check logic considers the QDrone flying to close to ground, too high or too low as well as generate a successful take off flag. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;A subset of the FSM monitoring signals are shown using this scope. These signals are what Quanser considers importnat for flight. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;FSM signals sent to the blackbox for post flight monitoring. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:12px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;Error message generation based on flags generated by the FSM signal checks. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</P>
    <P Name="Position">[-260, -162, 1315, -32]</P>
    <P Name="InternalMargins">[0, 0, 0, 0]</P>
    <P Name="HorizontalAlignment">left</P>
    <P Name="VerticalAlignment">top</P>
    <P Name="Interpreter">rich</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">-1</P>
  </Annotation>
  <Annotation SID="13856">
    <P Name="Name">7. Generate Warning Messages for User</P>
    <P Name="Position">[603, 635, 838, 885]</P>
    <P Name="InternalMargins">[0, 0, 0, 0]</P>
    <P Name="FixedHeight">on</P>
    <P Name="FixedWidth">on</P>
    <P Name="HorizontalAlignment">left</P>
    <P Name="VerticalAlignment">top</P>
